r←type AddDocLink name;i;pref;slug;order;c;cat
⍝ Add link to Dyalog documentation. Link to whichever object-reference category
⍝ actually has a page for this name, preferring the one implied by 'type' (e.g. the
⍝ Font property has no properties/ page but is documented under objects/). If the doc
⍝ source (DocsRoot) is unavailable, link unconditionally to the preferred category.

i←'class' 'prop' 'event' ⍳⊂type
'type must be ''class'', ''prop'' or ''event''' ⎕SIGNAL (4=i)/11
pref←i⊃'objects' 'properties' 'methodorevents'
slug←⎕C name
cat←pref

:If 2=⎕NC'DocsRoot'
:AndIf 0≠≢DocsRoot
    cat←''
    order←(⊂pref),('objects' 'properties' 'methodorevents')~⊂pref
    :For c :In order
        :If ⎕NEXISTS DocsRoot,c,'/',slug,'.md'
            cat←c ⋄ :Leave
        :EndIf
    :EndFor
    :If 0=≢cat ⋄ →0⊣r←name ⋄ :EndIf  ⍝ no Dyalog page in any category → plain text
:EndIf

r←'[',name,'](https://docs.dyalog.com/20.0/object-reference/',cat,'/',slug,'/)'
